---
/**
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SEEING.MD HOME PAGE
 * Route: /
 * Type: Page
 * Page version: 0.7.1 (reason clarification; SEEING.md 0.6.1)
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * PURPOSE
 * Introduces SEEING.md as a portable perception specification for people and
 * AI. Shows how unseen human assumptions can become decisions, systems, and
 * actions at scale, then gives visitors a direct way to use and help refine it.
 *
 * AUDIENCE AND PRIMARY ACTION
 * - Audience: Leaders, teams, AI practitioners, designers, developers,
 *   consultants, coaches, and individual practitioners
 * - Primary action: Get SEEING.md, then download from the Begin section
 * - Supporting action: Open Start Here for guidance or a human conversation
 * - Leader action: Request a private 30-minute Seeing First session, alone or
 *   with a team
 *
 * EXPERIENCE / STRUCTURE
 * Hero → Question → Missing layer → Example → Lens → Scope → Begin → Origin.
 * The three operating behaviors sit within the missing layer; usage instructions
 * are disclosed on demand. Seeing First follows the download as a quiet link.
 *
 * KEY RESPONSIBILITIES
 * - Serve the canonical specification from /SEEING.md.
 * - Give first-time visitors four plain-language ways to begin.
 * - Connect leaders to the Seeing First session through Cal.com.
 * - Connect the file to the deeper work at SEE DIFFERENT without obscuring the
 *   primary download action.
 *
 * DEPENDENCIES
 * - Layout: Standalone Astro page; no shared layout dependency
 * - Assets: Embedded open-frame SVG logo/favicon, Figma perception graphic,
 *   and the public copy of /SEEING.md
 * - Services: Google Fonts, Cal.com, and SEE DIFFERENT
 * - Hosting: Cloudflare Workers with Static Assets
 *
 * EDITING GUARDRAILS
 * - Preserve the Suede typography, spacing, black-and-white palette, and
 *   restrained use of #aa6600. Specifically:
 *   - Type scale: 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 24, 30, 36, 48, 60px. No rem, no
 *     intermediate sizes. Headings 500 weight; 600 reserved for real emphasis.
 *   - Spacing scale: 20, 30, 40, 60, 80, 100px.
 *   - Color: black, white, and #aa6600 only, through the opacity ladder tokens
 *     (80 / 60 / 50 / 15 / 10). Do not introduce grays or tinted panels.
 *   - Width axis: "wdth" 110 (--wdth-expanded) for display type and numerals.
 *     Standard width everywhere else.
 *   - Rules and borders at 1px. Reading measure 640px (--measure); composition
 *     width 1280px (--content).
 *   - Motion: 250ms interface, 500ms larger movement, ease-out, ~30px travel.
 * - Keep the downloadable specification synchronized with the canonical
 *   SEEING.md file at the repository root.
 * - Keep the Seeing First pathway distinct from downloading SEEING.md.
 * - Keep Start Here choices outcome-based and free of technical language.
 * - Do not imply that SEEING.md resolves every category of AI safety risk.
 * - Keep the book as the primary source and the DESIGN.md influence in the
 *   closing origin section rather than the opening argument.
 * - Keep external links secure with rel="noopener".
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

const title = 'SEEING.md — The Perception Behind Intent';
const description =
  'An open perception specification for examining what may shape intent—including its own assumptions—before AI carries it into action.';
