          <p class="section-number">The missing layer</p>
          <h2 id="why-title">We are trying to align AI with human intent without examining what shaped the intent.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="statement-body">
          <p><strong>AI isn’t the first system trained on the past. We are.</strong></p>
          <p>Before AI shapes an answer, prior experience has already helped shape what we ask, what we notice, and what we consider a good outcome.</p>
          <p><strong>AI didn’t introduce the lens.</strong> It can make the lens more powerful—and less visible.</p>
          <p>Before a system is designed, trained, evaluated, prompted, or deployed, people have already decided what matters, what the problem is, and what a good outcome looks like.</p>
          <p>Most of those decisions do not feel like decisions. They feel like reality.</p>
          <p>Reason may explain the decision without revealing what made the decision seem reasonable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="outcome-list">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Separate</h3><p>Fact from interpretation.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Surface</h3><p>What has already been assumed.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Ask</h3><p>The question the framing concealed.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="example-section" aria-labelledby="example-title">
        <div class="example-grid">
          <div>
            <h2 id="example-title" class="example-label">The brief</h2>
            <p class="example-text">Reduce the time our support team spends on customer complaints.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="example-label">What has already been decided?</h3>
            <p class="example-text">That time spent on complaints is the problem.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="example-question">Should the assistant reduce handling time, help identify unmet needs, or support both?</p>
      </section>

      <section class="lens" aria-labelledby="lens-title">
        <h2 id="lens-title">A <span>lens.</span> Not the lens.</h2>
        <p>Any insight about perception that cannot question itself eventually becomes another lens.</p>
        <p class="lens-note">An alternative framing is something to examine, not something to adopt.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="scope" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
        <h2 id="scope-title">Upstream, not all-encompassing.</h2>
        <div class="scope-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>It addresses</h3>
            <p>Human assumptions entering purpose, data, measures, prompts, evaluation, and use.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>It does not prevent</h3>
            <p>Autonomous behavior, malicious use, cyberattacks, deception, or loss of control.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="use" id="use" aria-labelledby="use-title">
        <p class="section-number">Begin</p>
        <h2 id="use-title">What shaped the intent?</h2>
        <p class="use-intro">Add SEEING.md to an AI conversation, brief, or project.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/SEEING.md" download onclick="window.fathom?.trackEvent('SEEING.md download');">Download SEEING.md <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="use-note">Then ask the AI to read it before consequential work involving people, judgment, strategy, or interpretation.</p>
        <details class="usage-details">
          <summary>How to use it</summary>
          <div class="instruction">
            <h3>In a conversation</h3>
            <p>Attach the file, then ask:</p>
            <blockquote>Read SEEING.md before responding. Apply it when the work involves people, judgment, strategy, interpretation, or a consequential decision. Question what may be shaping the request, including the assumptions this file brings to the inquiry.</blockquote>
          </div>
          <div class="instruction">
            <h3>For repeated project use</h3>
            <p>Add the file to your project and include this in its instructions:</p>
            <blockquote>Before work involving judgment, people, strategy, interpretation, or consequential decisions, read SEEING.md. Use it to examine the request, including the assumptions in SEEING.md, before acting. Apply it proportionally; do not slow straightforward technical work unnecessarily.</blockquote>
          </div>
          <p class="use-note">The file may not be read automatically. AI can help surface assumptions; people examine them and remain responsible for what is acted upon.</p>
        </details>
        <div class="orientation">
          <p class="orientation-steps"><span>Notice <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span> <span>Question <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span> <span>See Again <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span> <span>Act</span></p>
          <p>An orientation, not a formula.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="seeing-first" id="seeing-first">
          <p>Want to experience this with a real decision?</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://cal.com/billfox/seeing-first" rel="noopener">Seeing First <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="origin" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
        <p class="section-number">Origin</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="origin-title">The file is open. The practice is relational.</h2>
          <p>SEEING.md emerged from <em>The Perception Miracle</em> and more than 500 explorations into how the past enters what we see now.</p>
          <p>Its form was influenced by Brian Gardner’s DESIGN.md. SEEING.md asks the question one level further upstream: What shaped the intent?</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="text-link" href="https://seedifferent.xyz/perception-miracle/" rel="noopener">The Perception Miracle <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
